WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:09.330
End a lease early or at term, deduct what is owed from the deposit and print the settlement statement.

2
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:15.350
When a tenant leaves, settle the lease so everyone agrees on what is owed.

3
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:26.900
Choose End lease. You can end it quickly here, or settle it properly.

4
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.390
Choose End and settle.

5
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:37.660
Say whether the term is complete or the lease ends early, and the last day.

6
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:42.730
Decide whether to charge the early-exit penalty in the lease.

7
00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:48.160
List what comes off the deposit, such as repairs.

8
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.650
Choose how the rest is refunded.

9
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.170
Choose Work out the settlement.

10
00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:04.450
The statement nets the unpaid invoices, the penalties and the deductions against the deposit.

11
00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:11.040
Print it for the tenant to sign, and keep the handover papers with it.

12
00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:18.830
Then confirm. The lease ends, future invoices are voided, the refund is recorded and the units become available.
